Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop when freedesktop-sdk resolves setuptools-scm git-describe timeouts at the fdsdk level.
Subject: python3-vcs-versioning: bypass git-describe with SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION

Companion to 0006. Same reasoning: the ref-format: git-describe patch
(0005) does not actually push tag refs into the sandbox, so git describe
--match 'vcs-versioning-*' still has nothing to match and can hit the
40s subprocess timeout. The current element is racy — build 5 happened
to win the race, so 0005 looks like it worked, but the fix is not
structural.

Setting SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_VCS_VERSIONING skips VCS
detection entirely. Version picked to match the element's existing ref
(vcs-versioning-v2.6.0-0-gfa5c2319...).

Resolves: setuptools-scm#957 (upstream-documented workaround).

diff --git a/elements/components/python3-vcs-versioning.bst b/elements/components/python3-vcs-versioning.bst
--- a/elements/components/python3-vcs-versioning.bst
+++ b/elements/components/python3-vcs-versioning.bst
@@ -14,6 +14,10 @@ depends:
 variables:
   command-subdir: vcs-versioning

+environment:
+  # setuptools-scm#957 workaround: skip git-describe (times out in sandbox).
+  SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_VCS_VERSIONING: "2.6.0"
+
 sources:
 - kind: git_repo
   url: github:pypa/setuptools_scm.git
